  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t10-q04",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability.t1",
  "stem": {
   "en": "A card is drawn from a pack of 52. The events \"a heart\" and \"a king\" are:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "mutually exclusive"
   },
   {
    "en": "exhaustive"
   },
   {
    "en": "complementary"
   },
   {
    "en": "not mutually exclusive"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 3,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "The king of hearts belongs to both, so they can occur together."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t10-q05",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability.t2",
  "stem": {
   "en": "Two dice are thrown. The probability that the sum is 7 is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "1/6"
   },
   {
    "en": "5/36"
   },
   {
    "en": "1/12"
   },
   {
    "en": "7/36"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 0,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "Favourable: (1,6), (2,5), (3,4), (4,3), (5,2), (6,1) = 6 of 36. P = 6/36 = 1/6."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t10-q06",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability.t2",
  "stem": {
   "en": "In the statistical (empirical) definition, probability is the:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "set of all outcomes"
   },
   {
    "en": "ratio of favourable to total equally likely cases"
   },
   {
    "en": "number of favourable cases"
   },
   {
    "en": "limit of the relative frequency as the number of trials becomes very large"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 3,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "Von Mises: P(A) = lim m/n as n → ∞, where m is the number of times A occurs in n trials."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t10-q07",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability.t2",
  "stem": {
   "en": "Which of these is one of the axioms of probability?"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "P(A) > 1 for some A"
   },
   {
    "en": "P(A ∩ B) = P(A) + P(B)"
   },
   {
    "en": "P(A) = 0 for every A"
   },
   {
    "en": "P(S) = 1"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 3,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "The axioms: P(A) ≥ 0, P(S) = 1, and P(A ∪ B) = P(A) + P(B) for mutually exclusive A and B."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t10-q08",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability.t2",
  "stem": {
   "en": "A bag has 5 red and 3 black balls. Two balls are drawn at random. The probability that both are red is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "5/8"
   },
   {
    "en": "3/28"
   },
   {
    "en": "5/14"
   },
   {
    "en": "25/64"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 2,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "C(5, 2)/C(8, 2) = 10/28 = 5/14."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t10-q09",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability.t2",
  "stem": {
   "en": "Three cards are drawn from a well-shuffled pack of 52. The probability that all three are kings is:"
  },
  "options": [
