    "en": "3/52"
   },
   {
    "en": "1/5525"
   },
   {
    "en": "1/221"
   },
   {
    "en": "1/2197"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "C(4, 3)/C(52, 3) = 4/22100 = 1/5525."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t10-q10",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability.t3",
  "stem": {
   "en": "If P(A) = 0.5, P(B) = 0.4 and P(A ∩ B) = 0.2, then P(A ∪ B) is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "0.7"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.9"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.2"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.3"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 0,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "P(A ∪ B) = 0.5 + 0.4 − 0.2 = 0.7."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t10-q11",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability.t3",
  "stem": {
   "en": "If A and B are mutually exclusive, P(A ∪ B) equals:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "P(A) + P(B) − P(A)P(B)"
   },
   {
    "en": "1 − P(A)"
   },
   {
    "en": "P(A)P(B)"
   },
   {
    "en": "P(A) + P(B)"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 3,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "For mutually exclusive events P(A ∩ B) = 0, so P(A ∪ B) = P(A) + P(B)."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t10-q12",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability.t3",
  "stem": {
   "en": "If P(A) = 0.35, then P(A′) is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "0.65"
   },
   {
    "en": "1.35"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.5"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.35"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 0,
  "explanation": {
