  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t10-q13",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability.t3",
  "stem": {
   "en": "A card is drawn from a pack of 52. The probability that it is a king or a heart is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "17/52"
   },
   {
    "en": "1/52"
   },
   {
    "en": "4/13"
   },
   {
    "en": "1/4"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 2,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "P(K) + P(H) − P(K of hearts) = 4/52 + 13/52 − 1/52 = 16/52 = 4/13."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t10-q14",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability.t4",
  "stem": {
   "en": "If P(A ∩ B) = 0.12 and P(A) = 0.4, then P(B | A) is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "0.28"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.3"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.52"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.048"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "P(B | A) = P(A ∩ B)/P(A) = 0.12/0.4 = 0.3."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t10-q15",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-10-probability.t4",
  "stem": {
   "en": "A and B are independent with P(A) = 0.3 and P(B) = 0.5. Then P(A ∩ B) is:"
